  "tagline": "ByteDance's cloud-native ClickHouse fork with separated storage; archived in 2026.",
  "description": "ByConity was an open-source data warehouse from ByteDance's Volcano Engine, built on the ClickHouse 21.8 codebase and re-architected for storage-compute separation: data on HDFS or S3, stateless virtual warehouses, a FoundationDB-backed catalog, a cascades optimizer and ACID transactions. It was a notable experiment in making ClickHouse cloud-native. In 2026 Volcano Engine ended the project: a maintenance-only transition began on 1 June 2026, and the GitHub repository was archived after 1 August 2026 with no further fixes. Existing users should plan a migration.",
